# Neuroljus Care OS Design System

Public pages use one visual language: **deployable care infrastructure**, not a marketing site.

## Core palette (Care OS)

- Background: `#09090b` (page), `#0c0c0e` (panels), `#18181b` (console header)
- Borders: `#27272a`, `#3f3f46`
- Text primary: `#fafafa` · secondary: `#a1a1aa` · dim: `#71717a`
- Terminal accent: `#3ecf9a` (active, links, CTAs on dark)
- Warning: `#fbbf24` · danger: `#f87171`
- Sans: `ui-sans-serif, system-ui, …` for UI chrome
- Mono: `ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas` for protocol/console layers

## Layout patterns

- Status bar top: `neuroljus://local · care_command_protocol_v0 · audit=on · network=off`
- Nav: `NEUROLJUS / Platform name` + module pills (runtime, protocol, adapters, audit)
- Hero: CLI prompt (`$ neuroljus status --all`) + large headline + one subline
- Metrics strip: 4 numbers in monospace
- Console block: sidebar tabs + protocol stream (monospace)
- Module cards: `MOD.*` id, title, path link
- CTA band: green border + `OPEN WORKSPACE` button

## Care Room exception

Inside labs/future-care-room, the **scene** may stay warm (SVG room) but the **page chrome** should match Care OS dark frame where possible.

## Hard rules

- Present tense copy: "the robot receives", not "a future robot would receive"
- No purple kickers, no light-gradient landing backgrounds, no stock Tailwind on public pages
- Trilingual: every user-facing string in SV / EN / ES
- `prefers-reduced-motion` for animations
- No medical or diagnostic claims; caregiver always in charge
